<p>A queue holds work to be done later. A <strong>job</strong> runs once and leaves the queue; a <strong>task</strong> is a job with
a schedule, which stays and runs again each time it comes due. Both are stored through an adapter —
Redis, a database table, files on disk, memory or SQS — and both are executed by a worker, whether that
is a cron entry firing once a minute or a long-running daemon.</p>
<div class="code-window" x-data="copyCode">
